{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f'$", "MATH_0002": "$\\eta' \\in S'$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "MATH_0004": "$g$", "MATH_0005": "$\\eta = g(\\eta')$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\eta$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$\\eta'$", "MATH_0010": "$f'$", "MATH_0011": "$f'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-dominant}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-points-fibre-product}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-dominant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:69d5207dd00374c0eaef898aab2cce59bda926a22e830997e489cebcfd0533f5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d9c9706212ca075b3c227699f62231581c59943d1a6cd3986ef9d3cc46974133", "source_text": "Observe that <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact by Schemes, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be the generic point of an irreducible\ncomponent of <MATH_0003>. If generalizations lift along <MATH_0004>,\nthen <MATH_0005> is the generic point of an irreducible\ncomponent of <MATH_0006>. By Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe see that <MATH_0007> is in the image of <MATH_0008>.\nHence <MATH_0009> is in the image of <MATH_0010> by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nIt follows that <MATH_0011> is dominant by Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d30956c90b0c0425ebe9900fb8a22aef39f208ae3acce0e1a3500c771e55581d", "unit_id": "tag:0H3F:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a4b765b91cf0347ca31501c857a112b069c6a920061a2dc7c5e1213a54baefd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nPart of this holds for arbitrary (not necessarily quasi-compact)\ndominant morphisms.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:00ebcdd198ec4c02666731890878faac6c7a6f28583f326e6fa24f7fc725b21b", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$g : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$g$", "MATH_0006": "$f'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-base-change-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:df294256a58d5b326db6f4f6459f6a2d990976dfc33d8bf6a5f1e8848db07b0c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:05ec74aa972f316e2a223b4f656ec80a064874262bdd5f045138e5bdc5477580", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a dominant morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an open morphism of schemes, and let <MATH_0003>\nbe the base change of <MATH_0004> by <MATH_0005>. Then <MATH_0006> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:30595d1ca210eca2325ccdd63054283ed4bba59b104aa1a0ea6983902e5a398c", "unit_id": "tag:0H8F:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f'$", "MATH_0002": "$f'(X')$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$S'$", "MATH_0005": "$S'-B$", "MATH_0006": "$S'$", "MATH_0007": "$g$", "MATH_0008": "$g(S'-B)$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$f(X)$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$x\\in X$", "MATH_0013": "$f(x) \\in g(S'-B)$", "MATH_0014": "$W = \\Spec(\\kappa (f(x)))$", "MATH_0015": "$X_W$", "MATH_0016": "$S_W$", "MATH_0017": "$S'_W$", "MATH_0018": "$S$", "MATH_0019": "$W$", "MATH_0020": "$X_W$", "MATH_0021": "$(S'-B)_W$", "MATH_0022": "$X_W \\times_W (S'-B)_W$", "MATH_0023": "$W$", "MATH_0024": "$f'(X \\times_S S')$", "MATH_0025": "$B \\subset S'$", "MATH_0026": "$f'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:442eecf581255520ca27bce8b7815f4daf6eb2f1844ae12f232f0ae26ea5be0e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2c5dcf90fed7176d0c7bb05526905f037049feff8512948e24f6b5087d1a800b", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is not dominant, then <MATH_0002> is contained in some closed\nsubset <MATH_0003> not equal to <MATH_0004>. Then <MATH_0005> is open in <MATH_0006> and nonempty.\nSince <MATH_0007> is open, <MATH_0008> is nonempty and open in <MATH_0009>. Since <MATH_0010>\nis dense in <MATH_0011>, there is a point <MATH_0012> with <MATH_0013>.\nLet <MATH_0014>,\nand write <MATH_0015>, <MATH_0016>, <MATH_0017> for the pullbacks\nof these schemes from <MATH_0018> to <MATH_0019>. Then <MATH_0020> and <MATH_0021> are nonempty,\nand so <MATH_0022> is nonempty, as <MATH_0023> is the spectrum\nof a field. This contradicts that <MATH_0024> is contained\nin <MATH_0025>. So in fact <MATH_0026> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11d894b7b8a89772d95877ed0f31494284e060b9f2c9466a3213dd1ff9d64ccc", "unit_id": "tag:0H8F:proof"}
